From: Wazo Support <support@wazo.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "pjsip: Eliminate some unique taskprocessors."

This reverts upstream commit 9f838868f8, first released in Asterisk
22.11.0. Outbound sessions and AOR OPTIONS handling go back to their own
serializers instead of the shared distributor serializers.

With the shared serializers, a channel masquerade suspending a
distributor serializer can deadlock with "module reload res_pjsip.so":
the reload waits on the suspended serializer while holding the taskpool
taskprocessor the masquerade needs to finish. All SIP processing stops.

Rebased on Asterisk 22.11.0 with the Wazo patch series.
